       "id": "bbe11b5c",
       "tag": "Remote/Day",
       "stem": "You are asked to anaesthetise a 55-year-old man with schizophrenia for his first electroconvulsive therapy (ECT). He has longstanding hypertension and hyperlipidaemia. After the first ECT, the psychiatrist requests for a longer duration of seizure for the subsequent ECTs.",
       "q": "Outline the physiological effects expected during ECT (25%). · Discuss your anaesthetic considerations and management. (60%) · Explain how you would alter your technique (15%)."
